WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.044 --> 00:00:01.718
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.718 --> 00:00:04.626
today's message is stay open.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:06.209
Over to you, Queen Latifah.

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:08.653
(rooster cawing)

00:00:08.653 --> 00:00:11.077
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.892
♫ Entpresso keep me going

00:00:13.892 --> 00:00:17.800
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.904
- You've won a Grammy, you've
got nominations for an Oscar,

00:00:20.904 --> 00:00:22.469
you've won a SAG award,
you've won a Golden Globe,

00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:24.207
but you've done so much.

00:00:24.207 --> 00:00:25.801
How do you keep going?

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.301
What inspires you?

00:00:28.612 --> 00:00:30.944
- Honestly, I pray always to stay open.

00:00:30.944 --> 00:00:33.330
You know, if you're always
learning something new,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.739
then, you can be inspired.

00:00:35.739 --> 00:00:37.921
But I don't just kind of
sit and look at the past,

00:00:37.921 --> 00:00:40.365
like I did this, until
people like you remind me

00:00:40.365 --> 00:00:42.665
of a lot of stuff, I don't really

00:00:42.665 --> 00:00:45.085
think about it in the same way.

00:00:45.085 --> 00:00:48.281
Because I see the new
things on the horizon and

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:51.164
I don't feel like I have
to do the same thing

00:00:51.164 --> 00:00:52.114
over and over.

00:00:52.114 --> 00:00:54.957
I think if you're a creative person, then

00:00:54.957 --> 00:00:57.049
you kind of just have to follow your vibe.

00:00:57.049 --> 00:00:59.729
If an opportunity is there
for something interesting

00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:02.649
that kind of sparks that thing in you,

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:03.978
then you go for it.

00:01:03.978 --> 00:01:06.177
And I'm just kind of never
one of those people who

00:01:06.177 --> 00:01:07.733
felt like I couldn't do it.

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.776
I've got the right people
around me that I believe

00:01:09.776 --> 00:01:12.233
to do anything I put my mind to.

00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:15.053
- Well you do kind of master
everything that you've done.

00:01:15.053 --> 00:01:17.548
- I don't master it all, but
I persevere through it all

00:01:17.548 --> 00:01:21.163
and it gives me a chance to
find the next thing to work on.

00:01:21.163 --> 00:01:22.663
So, I'm a fighter.

00:01:23.921 --> 00:01:25.755
I know how to take them as
much as I can give them.

00:01:25.755 --> 00:01:27.624
So that's what we do.

00:01:27.624 --> 00:01:29.247
- So I think it's really
important for entrepreneurs

00:01:29.247 --> 00:01:31.875
that we stay really focused and stubborn

00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:34.329
on our one word, our
values, and the mission

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:35.771
and what we're trying to accomplish.

00:01:35.771 --> 00:01:38.899
What we will not tolerate in our life,

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:40.940
but be open to everything else.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.709
I think this is where people fall down.

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:45.770
I think people are too attached to the how

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.866
and not enough attached to the why.

00:01:47.866 --> 00:01:48.925
So let me explain.

00:01:48.925 --> 00:01:51.637
You want to start a
business, you want a ticket

00:01:51.637 --> 00:01:52.702
to some big heights, right.

00:01:52.702 --> 00:01:55.741
I want to help a billion
entrepreneurs with my business.

00:01:55.741 --> 00:01:57.119
I want to do it through Believe.

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:00.207
Those two things are non-negotiable.

00:02:00.207 --> 00:02:01.788
I want to have a big impact.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.689
I want to do something that
has the potential to help

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:06.085
a billion entrepreneurs.

00:02:06.085 --> 00:02:08.228
And I'm going to do it through Believe.

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.059
It's my one word, it's the
most important core value

00:02:10.059 --> 00:02:10.933
that I have.

00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:14.983
I'm not going to do it in a
way that puts people down.

00:02:14.983 --> 00:02:17.571
The goal is not that important
that I would trash people

00:02:17.571 --> 00:02:21.431
or throw stones at people
or make people look bad,

00:02:21.431 --> 00:02:22.649
to achieve my goal.

00:02:22.649 --> 00:02:24.159
That would actually be easier.

00:02:24.159 --> 00:02:26.025
If this was a negative
channel, if this was

00:02:26.025 --> 00:02:27.966
the 10 biggest failures
of all these people,

00:02:27.966 --> 00:02:30.386
if these are the 10 stupid
things that this person did,

00:02:30.386 --> 00:02:32.979
I would get a lot more views.

00:02:32.979 --> 00:02:36.130
Because in general, people
would rather laugh at somebody,

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.327
than try to build them up.

00:02:38.327 --> 00:02:39.860
Because we want to just
escape our own life,

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.259
and seeing how other
people have had failure,

00:02:42.259 --> 00:02:43.620
and how crappy their life is,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.142
it makes us feel better about ourselves.

00:02:45.142 --> 00:02:46.702
That's not what I want to build.

00:02:46.702 --> 00:02:48.420
Believe is too important to me.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.032
Those two things are non-negotiable.

00:02:51.032 --> 00:02:54.686
Big impact, a billion
entrepreneurs through Believe.

00:02:54.686 --> 00:02:56.686
Everything else is open.

00:02:57.526 --> 00:02:58.983
Right now it's through the book,

00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:00.642
it's through my website,
it's through social media,

00:03:00.642 --> 00:03:02.035
it's through my YouTube channel.

00:03:02.035 --> 00:03:04.422
Those are the main areas
that I'm focusing my time on.

00:03:04.422 --> 00:03:07.422
If YouTube stops allowing
me to have the impact

00:03:07.422 --> 00:03:09.408
that I'm looking for,
I'll move somewhere else.

00:03:09.408 --> 00:03:10.962
I'll stop doing the channel.

00:03:10.962 --> 00:03:13.857
If I can get way more impact

00:03:13.857 --> 00:03:17.128
through Believe, writing books,

00:03:17.128 --> 00:03:20.181
maybe that's where I start
focusing my attention.

00:03:20.181 --> 00:03:23.947
And I think too many of
you are focused to the how.

00:03:23.947 --> 00:03:26.130
Not stubborn and focused enough on the why

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.431
and what the big thing is.

00:03:27.431 --> 00:03:30.070
And too focused on the how.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.615
Well recognize that your how will change.

00:03:32.615 --> 00:03:35.831
If you look at the story of
any successful entrepreneur,

00:03:35.831 --> 00:03:37.696
you'll see that the how changed.

00:03:37.696 --> 00:03:39.369
The plan that they started with,

00:03:39.369 --> 00:03:42.041
is never the plan that gets you to where

00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:43.584
you end up having your ultimate goal.

00:03:43.584 --> 00:03:44.789
It always changes.

00:03:44.789 --> 00:03:46.632
That's not to say don't
plan, plan is important.

00:03:46.632 --> 00:03:48.802
It's not just go out and see what works.

00:03:48.802 --> 00:03:50.804
You have to have a plan.

00:03:50.804 --> 00:03:53.140
But understand that the
plan is going to change.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.717
And if you are not open, and you're stuck

00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:57.647
and only having it
happen through this plan,

00:03:57.647 --> 00:04:00.014
you're likely going to fail.

00:04:00.014 --> 00:04:01.147
This is especially an issue,

00:04:01.147 --> 00:04:03.418
when you start bringing
people on under you.

00:04:03.418 --> 00:04:05.671
My goal, with the people on my team,

00:04:05.671 --> 00:04:08.474
is I want to help a billion entrepreneurs

00:04:08.474 --> 00:04:11.161
and we're going to do it
through the value of belief.

00:04:11.161 --> 00:04:12.122
Give me ideas.

00:04:12.122 --> 00:04:13.247
How do we get there?

00:04:13.247 --> 00:04:15.154
Let me unlock your talents, your genius,

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.296
your creativity, to help me get there.

00:04:17.296 --> 00:04:18.620
Let's do this together.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.444
Because if all you're going
to do is exactly what I

00:04:20.444 --> 00:04:23.853
tell you to do, we're always
going to be restricted.

00:04:23.853 --> 00:04:25.958
You know, and I learned this
lesson in my first business

00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:28.651
where I spent too much
time planning and planning,

00:04:28.651 --> 00:04:31.055
and planning and planning.

00:04:31.055 --> 00:04:34.828
And I lost out on a huge
deal because I over planned.

00:04:34.828 --> 00:04:37.026
I think a lot of us get stuck on the how

00:04:37.026 --> 00:04:41.060
because we've invested
time, energy, effort, money

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.526
into one path.

00:04:42.526 --> 00:04:45.125
Which may ultimately
not be the path, right.

00:04:45.125 --> 00:04:48.567
I've bought lights and
I've got a camera man

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:50.878
and I've got editors and
I've got this team around

00:04:50.878 --> 00:04:51.896
building a YouTube channel.

00:04:51.896 --> 00:04:53.845
It'd be hard to walk away from.

00:04:53.845 --> 00:04:56.398
Especially when other people's
jobs are on the line as well.

00:04:56.398 --> 00:04:58.156
But if it's not helping me accomplish

00:04:58.156 --> 00:04:59.645
what I want to accomplish,
then I have to do it.

00:04:59.645 --> 00:05:01.214
I have to make that
tough decision to go off

00:05:01.214 --> 00:05:02.047
and do something else.

00:05:02.047 --> 00:05:03.886
Now, don't freak out.

00:05:03.886 --> 00:05:05.646
I'm not going anywhere,
YouTube is a great platform,

00:05:05.646 --> 00:05:07.077
I love it and this is amazing.

00:05:07.077 --> 00:05:09.091
I look forward to my filming
days and all you guys

00:05:09.091 --> 00:05:09.966
in the comments.

00:05:09.966 --> 00:05:12.263
But, if it came to that,
I might have to switch

00:05:12.263 --> 00:05:13.096
to something else.

00:05:13.096 --> 00:05:14.963
In my original plan,
YouTube wasn't part of it.

00:05:14.963 --> 00:05:17.539
I never wanted to be YouTube famous.

00:05:17.539 --> 00:05:18.421
It was through my website

00:05:18.421 --> 00:05:20.477
that all these things
were going to happen.

00:05:20.477 --> 00:05:23.808
And I adjusted because
I was getting a lot more

00:05:23.808 --> 00:05:26.221
awareness, a lot more
attraction, a lot more fun

00:05:26.221 --> 00:05:27.387
through the YouTube channel.

00:05:27.387 --> 00:05:29.370
And that may change again
in a year, two years,

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:31.031
five years, 20 years or never.

00:05:31.031 --> 00:05:33.364
Stubbornness around the why,

00:05:34.743 --> 00:05:37.906
stubbornness around
your one word core value

00:05:37.906 --> 00:05:40.715
and complete flexibility
and openness around

00:05:40.715 --> 00:05:42.872
everything else.

00:05:42.872 --> 00:05:44.065
That's the key.

00:05:44.065 --> 00:05:45.688
So the question today is I'm curious,

00:05:45.688 --> 00:05:47.857
what are the non-negotiables for you?

00:05:47.857 --> 00:05:49.689
What's the why for you?

00:05:49.689 --> 00:05:51.230
What's the big thing
you're trying to build

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.772
and what's your one word core value?

00:05:53.772 --> 00:05:56.345
Put it in the comment's below,
super curious to find out.

00:05:56.345 --> 00:05:57.439
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:05:57.439 --> 00:05:58.964
to Brenda and Bill Schreiner.

00:05:58.964 --> 00:06:00.480
Thank you guys so much for picking up

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.496
a copy of my book, Your One Word,

00:06:02.496 --> 00:06:03.828
it really means a lot to me.

00:06:03.828 --> 00:06:04.975
I hope you're learning
some good lessons that

00:06:04.975 --> 00:06:07.456
you're applying to your
business and to your life,

00:06:07.456 --> 00:06:09.194
and I appreciate the support.

00:06:09.194 --> 00:06:10.396
Thank you guys again for watching,

00:06:10.396 --> 00:06:12.225
I hope you have an amazing day!

00:06:12.225 --> 00:06:13.847
I believe in you and hope you continue to

00:06:13.847 --> 00:06:15.430
believe in yourself!

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:16.624
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:06:16.624 --> 00:06:19.012
for another shot of Entpresso.

00:06:19.012 --> 00:06:21.713
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:21.713 --> 00:06:25.213
♫ Entpresso keep me going

00:06:27.557 --> 00:06:29.771
- I think to secret to my career is

00:06:29.771 --> 00:06:31.912
I don't know what I can't do

00:06:31.912 --> 00:06:33.824
(interviewer laughs)

00:06:33.824 --> 00:06:36.182
There are times when I should probably sit

00:06:36.182 --> 00:06:39.601
and think do I really want
to jump out there with

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:42.229
Philip Seymour, I mean
with John C. Reilly,

00:06:42.229 --> 00:06:44.896
and sing The Night Chicago Died

00:06:46.229 --> 00:06:50.162
or do I really want to play
the blues with Little Ed.

00:06:50.162 --> 00:06:51.563
You know, you just do it.

00:06:51.563 --> 00:06:53.437
You just do these things.

00:06:53.437 --> 00:06:54.270
- [Interviewer] And you become,

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:56.395
the audience wants you to do these things.

00:06:56.395 --> 00:07:00.245
- Yes, I think what's,
I don't know what it is,

00:07:00.245 --> 00:07:02.762
but I think over the years,
people have gotten comfortable

00:07:02.762 --> 00:07:04.791
with the notion that

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:06.224
I try things.

00:07:06.224 --> 00:07:07.483
- [Interviewer] It's almost puntinesque

00:07:07.483 --> 00:07:09.673
- And they're not worried about me.

00:07:09.673 --> 00:07:10.553
Do you know what I mean?

00:07:10.553 --> 00:07:12.011
I think that's the key.

00:07:12.011 --> 00:07:15.920
People aren't worried
about me getting hurt

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.061
because,

00:07:17.061 --> 00:07:21.337
I can, you know, I'll
give it a hundred percent

00:07:21.337 --> 00:07:23.434
and then if it completely
falls on it's face,

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:25.201
I'll laugh about it an move on.

00:07:25.201 --> 00:07:27.044
And I think there's a little bit of sense

00:07:27.044 --> 00:07:29.877
after all these years,
people say, you know

00:07:29.877 --> 00:07:31.288
all right he tried it.

00:07:31.288 --> 00:07:33.002
Maybe it worked, maybe it didn't work,

00:07:33.002 --> 00:07:34.979
but he had a good time.

00:07:34.979 --> 00:07:37.113
- And for you, you can
come back the next night

00:07:37.113 --> 00:07:38.522
and the next night and the next night.

00:07:38.522 --> 00:07:40.355
- Yeah, I mean that's,

00:07:41.459 --> 00:07:43.450
you know, I don't know.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.367
There's a,

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.694
Over the years I've realized

00:07:48.694 --> 00:07:52.861
that there are a lot of
comedians that are very worried

00:07:54.422 --> 00:07:56.521
about keeping their dignity in tact.

00:07:56.521 --> 00:07:59.546
And keeping their personal space and

00:07:59.546 --> 00:08:01.435
keeping their sense of authority.

00:08:01.435 --> 00:08:03.862
And for better or worse,
and it might be worse,

00:08:03.862 --> 00:08:05.496
I don't have that.

00:08:05.496 --> 00:08:06.406
You know what I mean?

00:08:06.406 --> 00:08:10.115
The people that I've
always liked growing up,

00:08:10.115 --> 00:08:11.649
and I'm not just talking
about late night comedians.

00:08:11.649 --> 00:08:14.999
I'm talking about anybody
in movie, in film.

00:08:14.999 --> 00:08:17.716
The people I liked, Peter Sellers, they

00:08:17.716 --> 00:08:18.549
- Would let it all hang out.

00:08:18.549 --> 00:08:20.661
- Be just go, you know.

00:08:20.661 --> 00:08:23.193
If you look at a lot of those
old classic Carson clips,

00:08:23.193 --> 00:08:26.142
he's jumping into hot
tubs with Don Rickles,

00:08:26.142 --> 00:08:30.594
he's jumping through fake
walls, he's falling on his ass

00:08:30.594 --> 00:08:32.927
he's dressed as Floyd Turbo.

00:08:34.322 --> 00:08:37.282
And so sometimes I look back
to that and I remembered

00:08:37.282 --> 00:08:39.782
well, Johnny just went for it,

00:08:40.729 --> 00:08:44.896
So for better or worse, I'll
try, I'll get out there.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.480
I'm very physical and my
wife is always horrified.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.888
I'm always coming out of
the shower just covered

00:08:50.888 --> 00:08:52.667
in bruises and she'll say what was that?

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:54.198
And I'll say, Oh, I did a bit,

00:08:54.198 --> 00:08:57.241
we had Jeff Garlin on
the show and he and I

00:08:57.241 --> 00:09:01.719
rolled down a flight of steps
and I hit a fire hydrant.

00:09:01.719 --> 00:09:03.804
- And I achieved the goals I wanted

00:09:03.804 --> 00:09:08.745
in the Karate world, in the
world title and my schools.

00:09:08.745 --> 00:09:12.465
And I was trying to
decide what new energies,

00:09:12.465 --> 00:09:16.416
where I wanted to direct
my energies at and

00:09:16.416 --> 00:09:18.903
Steve McQueen, who was one of my students,

00:09:18.903 --> 00:09:22.625
at the time, suggested the acting field.

00:09:22.625 --> 00:09:24.347
And I just had finished
a movie with Bruce Lee,

00:09:24.347 --> 00:09:26.027
called Return of the Dragon.

00:09:26.027 --> 00:09:28.162
So I decided that I would pursue that.

00:09:28.162 --> 00:09:31.579
- Have a mind that is open to everything,

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:35.339
and attached to nothing.

00:09:36.372 --> 00:09:38.630
One of the central
principles of my life is

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:42.213
that no one knows enough
to be a pessimist,

00:09:43.718 --> 00:09:45.211
about anything.

00:09:45.211 --> 00:09:48.128
And that each and every one of us,

00:09:48.128 --> 00:09:52.808
when we close our mind to
what is possible for us

00:09:52.808 --> 00:09:55.281
or what is possible for humanity,

00:09:55.281 --> 00:09:57.114
closes off the genius,

00:09:59.322 --> 00:10:01.717
that resides and lives

00:10:01.717 --> 00:10:03.722
in each and every one of us.

00:10:03.722 --> 00:10:07.324
Having an open mind
doesn't necessarily mean

00:10:07.324 --> 00:10:09.731
finding fault with all of the things

00:10:09.731 --> 00:10:11.584
that you've been taught by others.

00:10:11.584 --> 00:10:14.217
It means, opening yourself up

00:10:14.217 --> 00:10:17.683
to the potentiality and the possibility

00:10:17.683 --> 00:10:19.992
that anything and everything is possible.

